eived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688"}]},{"sha":"20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDIwYTU5ZTBkMzJiZmUxMDY1YmZmZTcyZTkzNDQyMmI3ZTg3ZTY2ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"yanki-m","email":"yanki@caura.ai","date":"2026-08-23T07:29:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-23T07:29:52Z"},"message":"docs: four README references that point at things which do not exist (#877)\n\nAll four broke on the 2026-08-15 repo rename. None is a legacy name kept\non purpose — they are wrong, not old.\n\n| Line | Was | Now |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 61, 132 | `cd caura-memclaw` | `cd caura` |\n| 770 | `caura-memclaw-db-1` | `caura-db-1` |\n| 1046 | `memclaw/` (tree root) | `caura/` |\n| 1267 | `#how-memclaw-compares` | `#how-caura-compares` |\n\n**The quickstart is the one that matters.** Both `cd caura-memclaw`\nlines follow `git clone https://github.com/caura-ai/caura.git`, so the\nquickstart dies at its second line for every reader. It passes locally\nonly where a `caura-memclaw -> caura` symlink survived the rename, which\nis why it has gone unnoticed since 08-15. The 2026-08-19 rebrand audit\nflagged it as \"a functional break\".\n\nThe others: compose derives its project name from the directory, so a\nfresh clone gets `caura-db-1` and the `pg_dump` step names a container\nthat will not exist; the heading has read `## How Caura compares` (L415)\nsince the rename, leaving the L1267 anchor dead.\n\n## What this deliberately does not touch\n\nThe other 59 occurrences stay. `MEMCLAW_*` envs, the `memclaw` Postgres\nrole and database, the plugin and skill id, the `memclaw-client` /\n`MemClaw` aliases, the `ghcr.io/caura-ai/caura-memclaw-*` image names\n(verified against `docker-compose.yml`) and the `/memclaw/` routes are\nlive contracts under hard rule 3 — old names stay readable forever. They\ncome out with the env dual-read and infra waves, not with a prose sweep.\n\nLine 377's `npm install caura` claim is the fifth broken reference and\nis already fixed by #876; this branch leaves it alone to avoid the\nconflict.\n\n## Ratchet\n\n`scripts/legacy_name_ratchet.py` reports `No new lines. 4 removed by\nthis change (-4 net).`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Yanki <yanki@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"581f0d8409741a81ce18af416ed979b76f47bf8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/581f0d8409741a81ce18af416ed979b76f47bf8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiqFwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV/kQAIke9fbKpYWKgVfvUuTAt1zw\n2UfXmpy+YWBFXim5QHA3CBo9+kzsHjTZqqEOkcPg6zgokC6Kf50IK4kFR2XRh2tI\nTiH12VtYwqwtJkGsUpigu6qWokEIRoUQUptKvhyDfKG1Z12qhXE5JB+NGdO7Ip6G\ndiquHn5SDrBxnl7/NxXXt9n39/Wiw8ekzU4CKS5kqNPtXY9AApArbTwLyh19bTFZ\nSdMSwmW5vNBQ6lGUnwmz/hQh8TwbT8f/TfVFFg6HSClQpJoJnv7PQ3BHb6oeH/op\nM1QfXjErnM7lYdEj5C7nQj8VVU8DquRw05310VRFbC6XWQehJV0/lMo41GXdRYXQ\n7VoVOthYb6KjXpRQvDGdPjzrg92lgKDz1jAAcY+kKFieKolr5QJ63jc6vegCJEBw\nWSZicXnxtYVUVa/SzvXj/coXFBMr9IfIg1I0oAToHSnf3/fw35IE2ajNGD8V/yia\nQYaCzX0eYkGTiLbxxZlEYA9F4jHtet4uRRI5t524MEISJ7hQXggjph/dr1x78qeX\n337WifBYzQrHPKEjk2ZYm7XtlbaHsMFTl1h5eugf9KZL1oE9DblzYyh8m91x6XDS\nl7HMttBVfg5tN7xvDniY/asy4V23Hd15nOGf8Q89jl+eU5pzbuFofvFMw21/iUxo\nBi+bDjJ6kqL6kLJjcXLm\n=lnby\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 581f0d8409741a81ce18af416ed979b76f47bf8d\nparent 0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2\nauthor yanki-m <yanki@caura.ai> 1787470192 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787470192 +0300\n\ndocs: four README references that point at things which do not exist (#877)\n\nAll four broke on the 2026-08-15 repo rename. None is a legacy name kept\non purpose — they are wrong, not old.\n\n| Line | Was | Now |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 61, 132 | `cd caura-memclaw` | `cd caura` |\n| 770 | `caura-memclaw-db-1` | `caura-db-1` |\n| 1046 | `memclaw/` (tree root) | `caura/` |\n| 1267 | `#how-memclaw-compares` | `#how-caura-compares` |\n\n**The quickstart is the one that matters.** Both `cd caura-memclaw`\nlines follow `git clone https://github.com/caura-ai/caura.git`, so the\nquickstart dies at its second line for every reader. It passes locally\nonly where a `caura-memclaw -> caura` symlink survived the rename, which\nis why it has gone unnoticed since 08-15. The 2026-08-19 rebrand audit\nflagged it as \"a functional break\".\n\nThe others: compose derives its project name from the directory, so a\nfresh clone gets `caura-db-1` and the `pg_dump` step names a container\nthat will not exist; the heading has read `## How Caura compares` (L415)\nsince the rename, leaving the L1267 anchor dead.\n\n## What this deliberately does not touch\n\nThe other 59 occurrences stay. `MEMCLAW_*` envs, the `memclaw` Postgres\nrole and database, the plugin and skill id, the `memclaw-client` /\n`MemClaw` aliases, the `ghcr.io/caura-ai/caura-memclaw-*` image names\n(verified against `docker-compose.yml`) and the `/memclaw/` routes are\nlive contracts under hard rule 3 — old names stay readable forever. They\ncome out with the env dual-read and infra waves, not with a prose sweep.\n\nLine 377's `npm install caura` claim is the fifth broken reference and\nis already fixed by #876; this branch leaves it alone to avoid the\nconflict.\n\n## Ratchet\n\n`scripts/legacy_name_ratchet.py` reports `No new lines. 4 removed by\nthis change (-4 net).`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nSigned-off-by: Yanki <yanki@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-23T07:29:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/20a59e0d32bfe1065bffe72e934422b7e87e6688/comments","author":{"login":"yanki-m","id":232570632,"node_id":"U_kgDODdy_CA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232570632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m","html_url":"https://github.com/yanki-m","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanki-m/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2"}]},{"sha":"0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDBhMmQ3Yzc3OTU5NzNiNDE0YzFkNWEwMjE2OTE1Nzg1MGZmYjZkYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eldad Dahan","email":"eldad@caura.ai","date":"2026-08-22T22:05:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-22T22:05:05Z"},"message":"ci(review): count conftest and shared test helpers as source, not just say so (#874)\n\nci(review): count conftest and shared test helpers as source, not just\nsay so\n\n#872 told the reviewer to review `conftest.py` and `tests/_*.py`. That\ninstruction lives in `REVIEW_PROMPT`, which is only read once the review\njob runs — and whether it runs is decided earlier, by `pre-checks`\ncondition 6:\n\n    SRC_FILES=$(gh api ... --jq '[.[] | select(.filename |\n      (startswith(\"tests/\") or ...) | not)] | length')\n    if [[ \"$SRC_FILES\" -eq 0 ]]; then skip\n\nBoth carved-out patterns start with `tests/`, so a pull request confined\nto them still counted zero source files, the job skipped, and the new\nprompt was never reached. The half that shipped covers a real case — a\nPR\ntouching source AND `conftest.py` no longer has the conftest part\nignored\n— but the case it was written for stayed open.\n\nThis is the other half: those two patterns now count as source.\n\n## Why they earn it\n\n`tests/conftest.py` is the highest-fan-in file in the suite, and\n`tests/_scoped_module.py` is imported by five test files. A defect in\neither is a defect in everything downstream, which is the argument for\nreviewing source in the first place. The exclusion exists so a docs typo\ndoes not spend a review; it was never meant to cover the files most\ncapable of breaking the suite silently.\n\nThree of this month's PRs demonstrate the gap, and the third is the one\nworth stating plainly:\n\n  #866  tests/conftest.py only          -> skipped\n  #868  five test files + a new helper  -> skipped\n  #872  one workflow .yml               -> skipped\n\n**The pull request removing the exclusion was not reviewed, for the\nreason\nit existed to fix.** A `.yml` is config, so it too counted zero.\n\nNot widened further. Ordinary `test_*.py`, docs, lockfiles, Dockerfile,\nhelm and other workflow YAML still count zero, which is what keeps a\none-word README change from costing a review run.\n\n## The test runs the workflow's own expression\n\n`tests/test_review_source_filter.py` extracts the `--jq` argument from\n`claude_code_review.yml` and executes it against fixture file lists. It\ndoes not restate it.\n\nThat is the whole point. A copy pins the copy: the two drift, the test\nstays green, and the expression deciding whether any code gets reviewed\ngoes back to being unverified — which is how this gap survived in the\nfirst place. Extraction also means rewording that step fails loudly\nhere,\nwith a message saying to fix the regex rather than delete the test.\n\n17 tests. Five fail against the merged state — the four shared-helper\npaths and the mixed-count case — and were confirmed to do so by\nreverting\nthe workflow hunk and re-running. The other twelve pass either way by\ndesign: they are the do-not-over-widen side, and a carve-out broad\nenough\nto catch the helpers by accident would break them.\n\n`jq` is preinstalled on GitHub runners; the module skips if it is absent\nlocally rather than failing.\n\n## Consequence to expect\n\nEvery conftest-touching pull request now spends a review run, including\ntrivial ones. That is the intended trade and it is worth naming, since\nit\nis a real cost per PR rather than a one-off.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"0f4510f176242431e0c879f3298621afda93cbeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/0f4510f176242431e0c879f3298621afda93cbeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqih0RCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgQkQAAvDQiMCujwzdnQD4edUqdum\nNR5wRYvZVPbjZWeSMy7dFHnMEz9U12Di2wFuWVuRw+z4FvBS1OpAdZV2+V6IxHFD\nEJ7DbtivPDesMgrV/B+jtlJe4KEzolsk0q8vGx7GJ+TjBsDufHxjeQpbWPqpj/e9\n1QNARMbiTojCWTpZS0gmszg3fsVE2mx0XK5SQlVHW3Ba7DhJuciVLBzMJy8TFo+Y\npTahROWIGt/OaAzp1OL+TuY+BnHEJV10B0hz3E0yYsfNriB+KnJPzhmlr5KsPEOK\n+QCiCmRty8Z2IFYy832P4DvGzMxhRzswiHe2t85zof2ghxAJdD48HDw2Sq9T78LH\naztuMtdq3k+lkijIuAQlRJeiV1TQfKfReAN1yup3E6UGP1Hj2awH4S6fmDZrgWcn\nWuH9IdPSWK8ehrNds4pNt5W64iBIT3PQVfG78k1RvWEFML6CoChOQ+SGr5nMcF7M\nyt2MzT3BsLiJLCGHwo/aOzsDWcXZ4ANaTYktqR/Gtfpcaaz3OecD8kQ2i8Nm26Zl\n6BrUtovXQtlGcM6Psb/kE/rUYF6qWTX/IHhdG9p2QHhHXPIyDnyInybgo7Mk0ceW\nLxhrdMERlBppKQV/3lejyUzd2fjvL3/n3Xp0Y8NhRudW2ABXsV1Nz3WfCy8B6xP0\n7Xnn8Z691p/XmTQFeyPm\n=pocI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f4510f176242431e0c879f3298621afda93cbeb\nparent f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c\nauthor Eldad Dahan <eldad@caura.ai> 1787436305 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787436305 +0300\n\nci(review): count conftest and shared test helpers as source, not just say so (#874)\n\nci(review): count conftest and shared test helpers as source, not just\nsay so\n\n#872 told the reviewer to review `conftest.py` and `tests/_*.py`. That\ninstruction lives in `REVIEW_PROMPT`, which is only read once the review\njob runs — and whether it runs is decided earlier, by `pre-checks`\ncondition 6:\n\n    SRC_FILES=$(gh api ... --jq '[.[] | select(.filename |\n      (startswith(\"tests/\") or ...) | not)] | length')\n    if [[ \"$SRC_FILES\" -eq 0 ]]; then skip\n\nBoth carved-out patterns start with `tests/`, so a pull request confined\nto them still counted zero source files, the job skipped, and the new\nprompt was never reached. The half that shipped covers a real case — a\nPR\ntouching source AND `conftest.py` no longer has the conftest part\nignored\n— but the case it was written for stayed open.\n\nThis is the other half: those two patterns now count as source.\n\n## Why they earn it\n\n`tests/conftest.py` is the highest-fan-in file in the suite, and\n`tests/_scoped_module.py` is imported by five test files. A defect in\neither is a defect in everything downstream, which is the argument for\nreviewing source in the first place. The exclusion exists so a docs typo\ndoes not spend a review; it was never meant to cover the files most\ncapable of breaking the suite silently.\n\nThree of this month's PRs demonstrate the gap, and the third is the one\nworth stating plainly:\n\n  #866  tests/conftest.py only          -> skipped\n  #868  five test files + a new helper  -> skipped\n  #872  one workflow .yml               -> skipped\n\n**The pull request removing the exclusion was not reviewed, for the\nreason\nit existed to fix.** A `.yml` is config, so it too counted zero.\n\nNot widened further. Ordinary `test_*.py`, docs, lockfiles, Dockerfile,\nhelm and other workflow YAML still count zero, which is what keeps a\none-word README change from costing a review run.\n\n## The test runs the workflow's own expression\n\n`tests/test_review_source_filter.py` extracts the `--jq` argument from\n`claude_code_review.yml` and executes it against fixture file lists. It\ndoes not restate it.\n\nThat is the whole point. A copy pins the copy: the two drift, the test\nstays green, and the expression deciding whether any code gets reviewed\ngoes back to being unverified — which is how this gap survived in the\nfirst place. Extraction also means rewording that step fails loudly\nhere,\nwith a message saying to fix the regex rather than delete the test.\n\n17 tests. Five fail against the merged state — the four shared-helper\npaths and the mixed-count case — and were confirmed to do so by\nreverting\nthe workflow hunk and re-running. The other twelve pass either way by\ndesign: they are the do-not-over-widen side, and a carve-out broad\nenough\nto catch the helpers by accident would break them.\n\n`jq` is preinstalled on GitHub runners; the module skips if it is absent\nlocally rather than failing.\n\n## Consequence to expect\n\nEvery conftest-touching pull request now spends a review run, including\ntrivial ones. That is the intended trade and it is worth naming, since\nit\nis a real cost per PR rather than a one-off.\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>\n\nSigned-off-by: eldad-caura <eldad@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-08-22T22:05:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/0a2d7c7795973b414c1d5a02169157850ffb6dc2/comments","author":{"login":"Eldad-Caura","id":250841599,"node_id":"U_kgDODvOJ_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250841599?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura","html_url":"https://github.com/Eldad-Caura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Eldad-Caura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c"}]},{"sha":"f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGY4Y2QwY2EyNjI3YjJjZGVjY2ViNTE5ZTA4ZjYxYmU0Yjc2M2U1OGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-08-22T21:36:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-22T21:36:52Z"},"message":"ci(review): stop excluding conftest.py and shared test helpers from review (#872)\n\nHandover §06 trap: the reviewer's blanket `tests/` exclusion means\n`tests/conftest.py` — the highest-fan-in file in the suite — can never\nget automated review (#866's 'No issues found' actually meant 'did not\nlook'). This carves out `conftest.py` and `tests/_*.py` shared helpers;\nordinary test files remain excluded.\n\n@erni-a green-and-ready per house rules.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SBz7XjfFPBfdz3sQSNLBbB\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c8e93deff97695a55b0d6c45c3ffe7e22fe70d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/3c8e93deff97695a55b0d6c45c3ffe7e22fe70d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqihZ0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWLcQAIYjfuQgCc2/mCl2d3idL+UE\ndf4vS38AU/oBvGxZVi8CLq/XWgy7ewyBcF07wp+V6MNRLfbaPp21hS4liemSbSrm\nVr8YQpB3mYwP53mEqNcdNhk0ehfAnpx8TMpJRbEbIexLr1VB1w1N4nuk0ZAQVIe1\n3NpsYnTlWhH7xtq6nNEDosOvbdnlAZgI6pRL5MOhEOtefxO0C59B/dhMq+7hToX1\nyXUoiua7W97n+hNK1bKJKF3uYk7hI7mSHLVZN26MPFeDHkJ2PokqlEm7XTiepFrR\n/Gfpct+VJZGG32tHfHNk0nSDvEryUaInDOdi5sL+72dCcqR+bWw4ryP6aVwOTqGA\norU1g+BoB81hhzKw2a/xmKH9kEGtDIO3xzutqN3yyYKJZxfR/e3NsUTpKGTOFqft\naYKQZIXFMgRy31vMpWjYAwSijxJECQwTib68fCSOII12dYg5sGrk67ZIsbpWuA9T\nB/ek7wXQ5Dzz+Mib8JGDqQIwtSJOKzF/YMj5m2ncWikmIEdtLSoRtrBnQurACKPx\nJw28CymuxbRLeu7gOGTjWSfaj7Oeiw+tkCMiPb01dftWYP2+hfKaLYZ8z1cTBnq9\ndN2kvpp+99iL6RJYARdXhjp/eH6nBOik+4WJ9QNMAtnbIi21Jy619PpLQXADwQr3\nITayq+RadOfNaxLkA+SO\n=9pRn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c8e93deff97695a55b0d6c45c3ffe7e22fe70d9\nparent 496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1787434612 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787434612 +0300\n\nci(review): stop excluding conftest.py and shared test helpers from review (#872)\n\nHandover §06 trap: the reviewer's blanket `tests/` exclusion means\n`tests/conftest.py` — the highest-fan-in file in the suite — can never\nget automated review (#866's 'No issues found' actually meant 'did not\nlook'). This carves out `conftest.py` and `tests/_*.py` shared helpers;\nordinary test files remain excluded.\n\n@erni-a green-and-ready per house rules.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SBz7XjfFPBfdz3sQSNLBbB\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-22T21:36:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/f8cd0ca2627b2cdecceb519e08f61be4b763e58c/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7"}]},{"sha":"496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKDQ5NmJhMGY4NThjZTk0MTBkYjlkYmU1NjFkMTRhOGQ5OWMzMTJlYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"erni-a","email":"erni@caura.ai","date":"2026-08-22T21:32:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-22T21:32:17Z"},"message":"chore(clients): 1.0.1 — ship the H-01 recall fix to the registries (#870)\n\nThe #835 fix is merged but unpublished — PyPI/npm still serve 1.0.0,\nwhose `recall()` returns empty memories for every SDK user (Python and\nTS). Version bump to 1.0.1 on both clients; the `caura` metapackage and\n`memclaw-client` shim need no change (`>=1.0.0` resolves forward).\n\nPublish plan after merge: `uv build && uv publish` in clients/python\n(needs a fresh PyPI token or Trusted Publishing — the Aug 17 token was\nto be revoked), `npm publish` in clients/typescript (OTP).\n\nHandover follow-up: this closes the gap between §04 'all ten highs\nmerged' and what users actually install.\n\n@erni-a green-and-ready per house rules.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SBz7XjfFPBfdz3sQSNLBbB\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc291ba9339b22f57b9f25f58df52ea02e089c4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/cc291ba9339b22f57b9f25f58df52ea02e089c4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqihVhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADPcQAJ3N5iaf/r5dFDz7b3al9sYn\nSsPMTyzh16mIbRGZBnT26uJTm/aFerHT0DFu3k88lIr7uxk/lA9UKXlsfKnW1Rto\nKnRBSTShexQwCjaukyplgrZYtvrpOCU4JawQrT9/RMNAJccEUk+x/iWcgt4Mq9MV\n3eMlTbjjQiwzdL6IFvXkmWir0iADsYiDI/OwDKN6em8BW2ghgbapSf26MPiWMXGV\nY1eUKquftKdJjh7JeFRaB5GyMMzdvoGyhGxifYatWVazdCH3Z4LUfrRLH66bfUeu\nvMRHIzS31zFIKzXOZoDhoYwgLb+g48ofa9avsPboohxiV/aIv7m6dA9p+2D2FfUC\ntYfxQ5mmNTAl4GyQURD6aP5+lDRkb6CC9sVDKd/F36FH25pvBrSyq2KSTUF2h8hA\no2HvoB3zlY7UceQMmoszfB6DXPpKGb6cd97CXk64aCicgpKaoW3kRg4wKvUGge+y\njLtfFYwAUyMa0omrM2CTIyAbfO+eWuqLR4G742gqHvUj0MbDgFyACUu5x7LxwR6T\nlUZaXMYI7s0ZWWUeCRK1szJIQtx8lX+VIqqKD0eOBt8dVpLKvyy6+g151QiFrgQM\n/wgCyzzWDataWHc86LmexFP5IEAWORcfA/0YdKkwlu2Ac3Q4qlwpzgeZwqm0YJfi\nxCSILyVgsaIFgh1K5koC\n=LD+g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cc291ba9339b22f57b9f25f58df52ea02e089c4c\nparent b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8\nauthor erni-a <erni@caura.ai> 1787434337 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787434337 +0300\n\nchore(clients): 1.0.1 — ship the H-01 recall fix to the registries (#870)\n\nThe #835 fix is merged but unpublished — PyPI/npm still serve 1.0.0,\nwhose `recall()` returns empty memories for every SDK user (Python and\nTS). Version bump to 1.0.1 on both clients; the `caura` metapackage and\n`memclaw-client` shim need no change (`>=1.0.0` resolves forward).\n\nPublish plan after merge: `uv build && uv publish` in clients/python\n(needs a fresh PyPI token or Trusted Publishing — the Aug 17 token was\nto be revoked), `npm publish` in clients/typescript (OTP).\n\nHandover follow-up: this closes the gap between §04 'all ten highs\nmerged' and what users actually install.\n\n@erni-a green-and-ready per house rules.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01SBz7XjfFPBfdz3sQSNLBbB\n\nSigned-off-by: erni <erni@caura.ai>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-22T21:32:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/496ba0f858ce9410db9dbe561d14a8d99c312ea7/comments","author":{"login":"erni-a","id":229583271,"node_id":"U_kgDODa8ppw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229583271?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a","html_url":"https://github.com/erni-a","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erni-a/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8"}]},{"sha":"b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGI2NWVjYmUxNzYwNWYyYTgwYWYzMTkwMjhlNzAzZTVlMzZjMGViYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-22T18:55:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-22T18:55:43Z"},"message":"deps: update structlog requirement from <26,>=25.4 to >=26.1.0,<27 (#633)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[structlog](https://github.com/hynek/structlog) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/releases\">structlog's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>26.1.0</h2>\n<h2>Highlights</h2>\n<p>Given how long this release took, it's pretty thicc with nice things\nall over the board! Apologies for the long release cycle; it's been a\nvictim of the slopocalypse and me trying to navigate my way thru the new\nnormal. Extra big thanks to my sponsors for not abandoning me in these\nunironically trying times. ❤️</p>\n<p><em>Full changelog below!</em></p>\n<h2>Special Thanks</h2>\n<p>This release would not be possible without my generous sponsors!\nThank you to all of you making sustainable maintenance possible! If\n<em>you</em> would like to join them, go to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/hynek\">https://github.com/sponsors/hynek</a>\nand check out the sweet perks!</p>\n<h3>Above and Beyond</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.variomedia.de/\">Variomedia AG</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/variomedia\">variomedia</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.tidelift.com/\">Tidelift</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tidelift\">tidelift</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://kraken.tech\">Kraken Tech</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kraken-tech\">kraken-tech</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.klaviyo.com\">Klaviyo</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/klaviyo\">klaviyo</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://privacy-solutions.org\">Privacy Solutions GmbH</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/privacy-solutions\">privacy-solutions</a>), <a\nhref=\"http://filepreviews.io/\">FilePreviews</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/filepreviews\">filepreviews</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://ecosyste.ms\">Ecosystems</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ecosyste-ms\">ecosyste-ms</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.lambdatest.com\">TestMu AI Open Source Office (Formerly\nLambdaTest)</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LambdaTest-Inc\">LambdaTest-Inc</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/about\">GitHub</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github\">github</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://doist.com/\">Doist</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Doist\">Doist</a>), Daniel Fortunov (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asqui\">asqui</a>), and Kevin P. Fleming (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kpfleming\">kpfleming</a>).</p>\n<h3>Maintenance Sustainers</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://buttondown.com\">Buttondown</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/buttondown\">buttondown</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://christopher.xyz\">Christopher Dignam</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/chdsbd\">chdsbd</a>), Magnus Watn (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/magnuswatn\">magnuswatn</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://cra.mr\">David Cramer</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dcramer\">dcramer</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://rivolaks.com\">Rivo Laks</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/rivol\">rivol</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://polar.sh\">Polar</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/polarsource\">polarsource</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://miketheman.dev\">Mike Fiedler</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/miketheman\">miketheman</a>), Duncan Hill (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cricalix\">cricalix</a>), Colin Marquardt (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cmarqu\">cmarqu</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://blog.journeythatcounts.nl\">Pieter Swinkels</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/swinkels\">swinkels</a>), Nick Libertini (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/libertininick\">libertininick</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://bmdphd.info/\">Brian M. Dennis</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crossjam\">crossjam</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asweigart/readal\">Al Sweigart</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asweigart\">asweigart</a>), Celebrity News AG\n(@<a href=\"https://github.com/celebritynewsag\">celebritynewsag</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://westervelt.com\">The Westervelt Company</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/westerveltco\">westerveltco</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://slafs.net\">Sławomir Ehlert</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/slafs\">slafs</a>), Mostafa Khalil (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/khadrawy\">khadrawy</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://fmularczyk.pl\">Filip Mularczyk</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mukiblejlok\">mukiblejlok</a>), Thomas Klinger\n(@<a href=\"https://github.com/thmsklngr\">thmsklngr</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://poehlmann.io\">Andreas Poehlmann</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ap--\">ap--</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://atbigelow.com\">August Trapper Bigelow</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/atbigelow\">atbigelow</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://noumenal.es/\">Carlton Gibson</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/carltongibson\">carltongibson</a>), and <a\nhref=\"https://roboflow.com\">Roboflow</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/roboflow\">roboflow</a>).</p>\n<h2>Full Changelog</h2>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Python 3.8 and 3.9 support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deprecated</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for <em>better-exceptions</em> is deprecated and will be\nremoved within a year. Use our Rich integration or copy-paste the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/2c059a0dc029d9370e1e4a6e9683063205bbb68f/src/structlog/dev.py#L488-L498\">one\nline of code you need</a>. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/802\">#802</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Python 3.15 support. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/813\">#813</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.dev.rich_monochrome_traceback</code> for Rich-based\nmonochrome exception rendering and add support for it throughout\n<code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> when the user asks for no\ncolors. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/794\">#794</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code> now has a <code>name</code>\nattribute which allows you to use it with the\n<code>structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name()</code> processor\n<em>without</em> using the standard library integration. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/786\">#786</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now supports\n<code>CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE</code> that adds the qualified\nimport name of the module of the callsite, or <code>__main__</code> if\nthe module is the entry point. This is only available for\n<em>structlog</em>-originated events since the standard library has no\nequivalent (except for the convention of setting the logger's name to\n<code>__name__</code>). <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/812\">#812</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.stdlib.BoundLogger</code> now has\n<code>is_enabled_for()</code> and <code>get_effective_level()</code>\nmethods that are snake_case aliases for its <code>isEnabledFor()</code>\nand <code>getEffectiveLevel()</code> methods. This makes it more\ncompatible with the native\n<code>structlog.typing.FilteringBoundLogger</code>, so you can swap\nconfigurations without changing your call sites. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/818\">#818</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> does not warn anymore\nwhen the <code>exception</code> key has a rendered value despite having\na fancy formatter configured. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/790\">#790</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">structlog's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/25.5.0...26.1.0\">26.1.0</a>\n- 2026-06-06</h2>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Python 3.8 and 3.9 support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deprecated</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for <em>better-exceptions</em> is deprecated and will be\nremoved within a year.\nUse our Rich integration or copy-paste the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/2c059a0dc029d9370e1e4a6e9683063205bbb68f/src/structlog/dev.py#L488-L498\">one\nline of code you need</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/802\">#802</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Python 3.15 support.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/813\">#813</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.dev.rich_monochrome_traceback</code> for Rich-based\nmonochrome exception rendering and add support for it throughout\n<code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> when the user asks for no\ncolors.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/794\">#794</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code> now has a <code>name</code>\nattribute which allows you to use it with the\n<code>structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name()</code> processor\n<em>without</em> using the standard library integration.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/786\">#786</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now supports\n<code>CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE</code> that adds the qualified\nimport name of the module of the callsite, or <code>__main__</code> if\nthe module is the entry point.\nThis is only available for <em>structlog</em>-originated events since\nthe standard library has no equivalent (except for the convention of\nsetting the logger's name to <code>__name__</code>).\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/812\">#812</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.stdlib.BoundLogger</code> now has\n<code>is_enabled_for()</code> and <code>get_effective_level()</code>\nmethods that are snake_case aliases for its <code>isEnabledFor()</code>\nand <code>getEffectiveLevel()</code> methods.\nThis makes it more compatible with the native\n<code>structlog.typing.FilteringBoundLogger</code>, so you can swap\nconfigurations without changing your call sites.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/818\">#818</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> does not warn anymore\nwhen the <code>exception</code> key has a rendered value despite having\na fancy formatter configured.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/790\">#790</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code>,\n<code>structlog.PrintLogger</code>, and\n<code>structlog.WriteLogger</code> now hold <em>weak</em> references to\nthe files they use for output.\nThis prevents their leakage in long-running processes that open many\nlogfiles, such as task executors that create a per-task\n<code>BytesLogger</code> or <code>WriteLogger</code>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/807\">#807</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.WriteLogger</code> is usable after unpickling.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/787\">#787</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now reports\nthe calling thread's id and name for async log methods, instead of the\nthread from the executor pool that runs the underlying sync logger.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/8174a86a2f14b5bd295eded733ff5fffc12aa173\"><code>8174a86</code></a>\nPrepare 26.1.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/f168bda84dca86d9658d7908c5fc87a313829b2b\"><code>f168bda</code></a>\ndocs: fix msgspec URL</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/34abbd9ddc160aca214e9de042346bb18e0ad6d9\"><code>34abbd9</code></a>\nupdate dev</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/212a69497e4f4eb93b94a324eaabf258ba1cf70e\"><code>212a694</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/820\">#820</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/0eef50d9dc1bead60be9dba02dc0caa6788c2d9f\"><code>0eef50d</code></a>\nstdlib: Add snake_case shims for isEnabledFor &amp; getEffectiveLevel\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/818\">#818</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/f194271d998edb9662c825adeca155e685345595\"><code>f194271</code></a>\ndocs/stdlib: be direct w/ advising against AsyncBoundLogger</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/72943b3e1e2995b36bc6ce4bb1a647ac23f4483c\"><code>72943b3</code></a>\nAdd a recipe for customizing exc dict formatting (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/817\">#817</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/fcdca9f56519282b0c80d99afdb6b27fd0f76ce2\"><code>fcdca9f</code></a>\nupdate dev</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/fe9858d37e7501e6c4ad37083d823ade427520b0\"><code>fe9858d</code></a>\ndocs: remove italics</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/ba1a17857a9634ec790370aa09effabbcab3e067\"><code>ba1a178</code></a>\nAdd CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/812\">#812</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/25.4.0...26.1.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: erni-a <erni@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"6316667ee89100b15eace3660e41b5620a5e5c5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/6316667ee89100b15eace3660e41b5620a5e5c5c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqifCvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuOEQAE2VIq0MJ1e8Y9rNuIYi9svU\nh5Pt/74W6Wxgg1Ege2W5EfBMDl/VeDdPqJ8ETskECIYlLroCEKge2zD1VS0ismwd\n/1+GaiAmS17RSKBFsWQOkEJC5b25M7admpSGuf/82yyXEwKyGXuAsUK6XDsilFjK\n9GwRWHHydjmdNGuAigt/IjQvdicXDnjQd2FsIUwE5ii91B63TftjPLg17dj3t+tP\naOP2lVyETjnrMviAesLHYW2bfHE/1jI8j7UUrH2tHZGKKf8Z2kGZRNc8kx/AvsBs\nEehWTCPyAZ4a3PgSFxh852LecGyKC5D3zz4wmWT+oQsALRMKtWSQW4nhriydVHDJ\n4rlK21EGuMgAfC8vRmZlCUPcaZEBdewa2ijlxgkyYYTO6e4ShfkpQ3M1UOcr8Bkw\nma7KYlS/K+hFT3xdnLy/mqMlnKOXA7In3OHjZZ8N5B1qnoITzJ5JvsEiBRdvQfEV\nHqwXe48dyNsWEYaVMSJTvaosN/i4HMqs4kEASe3g711HgVcNa0RWOoIcDI998UkC\n0zSAp/PABfYCW7h01Bidglc8yjFNSD4VM6gL4ER/rUNs3X2fsEPD9lx5y67gOfHS\nADda/lDjyKhi5j7MdBGkzH8BkF6kgK2kqdhBiAEBDuu0vZ3yAJNNqHp6gnUw2KIO\nb6k69FAXap5N8sdlDUVb\n=TAlc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6316667ee89100b15eace3660e41b5620a5e5c5c\nparent b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787424943 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787424943 +0300\n\ndeps: update structlog requirement from <26,>=25.4 to >=26.1.0,<27 (#633)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[structlog](https://github.com/hynek/structlog) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/releases\">structlog's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>26.1.0</h2>\n<h2>Highlights</h2>\n<p>Given how long this release took, it's pretty thicc with nice things\nall over the board! Apologies for the long release cycle; it's been a\nvictim of the slopocalypse and me trying to navigate my way thru the new\nnormal. Extra big thanks to my sponsors for not abandoning me in these\nunironically trying times. ❤️</p>\n<p><em>Full changelog below!</em></p>\n<h2>Special Thanks</h2>\n<p>This release would not be possible without my generous sponsors!\nThank you to all of you making sustainable maintenance possible! If\n<em>you</em> would like to join them, go to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sponsors/hynek\">https://github.com/sponsors/hynek</a>\nand check out the sweet perks!</p>\n<h3>Above and Beyond</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.variomedia.de/\">Variomedia AG</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/variomedia\">variomedia</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.tidelift.com/\">Tidelift</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tidelift\">tidelift</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://kraken.tech\">Kraken Tech</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kraken-tech\">kraken-tech</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.klaviyo.com\">Klaviyo</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/klaviyo\">klaviyo</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://privacy-solutions.org\">Privacy Solutions GmbH</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/privacy-solutions\">privacy-solutions</a>), <a\nhref=\"http://filepreviews.io/\">FilePreviews</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/filepreviews\">filepreviews</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://ecosyste.ms\">Ecosystems</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ecosyste-ms\">ecosyste-ms</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://www.lambdatest.com\">TestMu AI Open Source Office (Formerly\nLambdaTest)</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LambdaTest-Inc\">LambdaTest-Inc</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/about\">GitHub</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github\">github</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://doist.com/\">Doist</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Doist\">Doist</a>), Daniel Fortunov (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asqui\">asqui</a>), and Kevin P. Fleming (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/kpfleming\">kpfleming</a>).</p>\n<h3>Maintenance Sustainers</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://buttondown.com\">Buttondown</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/buttondown\">buttondown</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://christopher.xyz\">Christopher Dignam</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/chdsbd\">chdsbd</a>), Magnus Watn (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/magnuswatn\">magnuswatn</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://cra.mr\">David Cramer</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dcramer\">dcramer</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://rivolaks.com\">Rivo Laks</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/rivol\">rivol</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://polar.sh\">Polar</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/polarsource\">polarsource</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://miketheman.dev\">Mike Fiedler</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/miketheman\">miketheman</a>), Duncan Hill (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cricalix\">cricalix</a>), Colin Marquardt (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/cmarqu\">cmarqu</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://blog.journeythatcounts.nl\">Pieter Swinkels</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/swinkels\">swinkels</a>), Nick Libertini (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/libertininick\">libertininick</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://bmdphd.info/\">Brian M. Dennis</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/crossjam\">crossjam</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asweigart/readal\">Al Sweigart</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/asweigart\">asweigart</a>), Celebrity News AG\n(@<a href=\"https://github.com/celebritynewsag\">celebritynewsag</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://westervelt.com\">The Westervelt Company</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/westerveltco\">westerveltco</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://slafs.net\">Sławomir Ehlert</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/slafs\">slafs</a>), Mostafa Khalil (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/khadrawy\">khadrawy</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://fmularczyk.pl\">Filip Mularczyk</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mukiblejlok\">mukiblejlok</a>), Thomas Klinger\n(@<a href=\"https://github.com/thmsklngr\">thmsklngr</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://poehlmann.io\">Andreas Poehlmann</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ap--\">ap--</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://atbigelow.com\">August Trapper Bigelow</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/atbigelow\">atbigelow</a>), <a\nhref=\"https://noumenal.es/\">Carlton Gibson</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/carltongibson\">carltongibson</a>), and <a\nhref=\"https://roboflow.com\">Roboflow</a> (@<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/roboflow\">roboflow</a>).</p>\n<h2>Full Changelog</h2>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Python 3.8 and 3.9 support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deprecated</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for <em>better-exceptions</em> is deprecated and will be\nremoved within a year. Use our Rich integration or copy-paste the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/2c059a0dc029d9370e1e4a6e9683063205bbb68f/src/structlog/dev.py#L488-L498\">one\nline of code you need</a>. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/802\">#802</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Python 3.15 support. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/813\">#813</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.dev.rich_monochrome_traceback</code> for Rich-based\nmonochrome exception rendering and add support for it throughout\n<code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> when the user asks for no\ncolors. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/794\">#794</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code> now has a <code>name</code>\nattribute which allows you to use it with the\n<code>structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name()</code> processor\n<em>without</em> using the standard library integration. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/786\">#786</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now supports\n<code>CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE</code> that adds the qualified\nimport name of the module of the callsite, or <code>__main__</code> if\nthe module is the entry point. This is only available for\n<em>structlog</em>-originated events since the standard library has no\nequivalent (except for the convention of setting the logger's name to\n<code>__name__</code>). <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/812\">#812</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.stdlib.BoundLogger</code> now has\n<code>is_enabled_for()</code> and <code>get_effective_level()</code>\nmethods that are snake_case aliases for its <code>isEnabledFor()</code>\nand <code>getEffectiveLevel()</code> methods. This makes it more\ncompatible with the native\n<code>structlog.typing.FilteringBoundLogger</code>, so you can swap\nconfigurations without changing your call sites. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/818\">#818</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> does not warn anymore\nwhen the <code>exception</code> key has a rendered value despite having\na fancy formatter configured. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/790\">#790</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">structlog's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/25.5.0...26.1.0\">26.1.0</a>\n- 2026-06-06</h2>\n<h3>Removed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Python 3.8 and 3.9 support.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Deprecated</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for <em>better-exceptions</em> is deprecated and will be\nremoved within a year.\nUse our Rich integration or copy-paste the <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/blob/2c059a0dc029d9370e1e4a6e9683063205bbb68f/src/structlog/dev.py#L488-L498\">one\nline of code you need</a>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/802\">#802</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Python 3.15 support.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/813\">#813</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.dev.rich_monochrome_traceback</code> for Rich-based\nmonochrome exception rendering and add support for it throughout\n<code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> when the user asks for no\ncolors.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/794\">#794</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code> now has a <code>name</code>\nattribute which allows you to use it with the\n<code>structlog.stdlib.add_logger_name()</code> processor\n<em>without</em> using the standard library integration.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/786\">#786</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now supports\n<code>CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE</code> that adds the qualified\nimport name of the module of the callsite, or <code>__main__</code> if\nthe module is the entry point.\nThis is only available for <em>structlog</em>-originated events since\nthe standard library has no equivalent (except for the convention of\nsetting the logger's name to <code>__name__</code>).\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/812\">#812</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.stdlib.BoundLogger</code> now has\n<code>is_enabled_for()</code> and <code>get_effective_level()</code>\nmethods that are snake_case aliases for its <code>isEnabledFor()</code>\nand <code>getEffectiveLevel()</code> methods.\nThis makes it more compatible with the native\n<code>structlog.typing.FilteringBoundLogger</code>, so you can swap\nconfigurations without changing your call sites.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/818\">#818</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer</code> does not warn anymore\nwhen the <code>exception</code> key has a rendered value despite having\na fancy formatter configured.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/790\">#790</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.BytesLogger</code>,\n<code>structlog.PrintLogger</code>, and\n<code>structlog.WriteLogger</code> now hold <em>weak</em> references to\nthe files they use for output.\nThis prevents their leakage in long-running processes that open many\nlogfiles, such as task executors that create a per-task\n<code>BytesLogger</code> or <code>WriteLogger</code>.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/807\">#807</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.WriteLogger</code> is usable after unpickling.\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/787\">#787</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><code>structlog.processors.CallsiteParameterAdder</code> now reports\nthe calling thread's id and name for async log methods, instead of the\nthread from the executor pool that runs the underlying sync logger.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/8174a86a2f14b5bd295eded733ff5fffc12aa173\"><code>8174a86</code></a>\nPrepare 26.1.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/f168bda84dca86d9658d7908c5fc87a313829b2b\"><code>f168bda</code></a>\ndocs: fix msgspec URL</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/34abbd9ddc160aca214e9de042346bb18e0ad6d9\"><code>34abbd9</code></a>\nupdate dev</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/212a69497e4f4eb93b94a324eaabf258ba1cf70e\"><code>212a694</code></a>\n[pre-commit.ci] pre-commit autoupdate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/820\">#820</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/0eef50d9dc1bead60be9dba02dc0caa6788c2d9f\"><code>0eef50d</code></a>\nstdlib: Add snake_case shims for isEnabledFor &amp; getEffectiveLevel\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/818\">#818</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/f194271d998edb9662c825adeca155e685345595\"><code>f194271</code></a>\ndocs/stdlib: be direct w/ advising against AsyncBoundLogger</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/72943b3e1e2995b36bc6ce4bb1a647ac23f4483c\"><code>72943b3</code></a>\nAdd a recipe for customizing exc dict formatting (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/817\">#817</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/fcdca9f56519282b0c80d99afdb6b27fd0f76ce2\"><code>fcdca9f</code></a>\nupdate dev</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/fe9858d37e7501e6c4ad37083d823ade427520b0\"><code>fe9858d</code></a>\ndocs: remove italics</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/commit/ba1a17857a9634ec790370aa09effabbcab3e067\"><code>ba1a178</code></a>\nAdd CallsiteParameter.QUAL_MODULE (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/hynek/structlog/issues/812\">#812</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/25.4.0...26.1.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: erni-a <erni@caura.ai>","verified_at":"2026-08-22T18:55:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b65ecbe17605f2a80af319028e703e5e36c0ebc8/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/commits/b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc","html_url":"https://github.com/caura-ai/caura/commit/b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc"}]},{"sha":"b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc","node_id":"C_kwDOSOAAX9oAKGIxNjU3YTRmMmY2MGI0MmRmMGZmN2EwYjBmNjFhOWYxYTRkOGU3YmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-22T18:50:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-22T18:50:42Z"},"message":"deps: update croniter requirement from >=2.0 to >=6.2.4 (#636)\n\nUpdates the requirements on\n[croniter](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter) to permit the latest\nversion.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/releases\">croniter's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4</h2>\n<h2>croniter 6.2.4</h2>\n<h3>Bugfixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>expand_from_start_time</code> day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges\n(<code>isoweekday() % 7</code> instead of <code>weekday() + 1</code>).\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239\">#239</a>,\nthanks <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/alhudz\"><code>@​alhudz</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Packaging</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Install:</strong> <code>pip install croniter==6.2.4</code> ·\n<a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/croniter/6.2.4/\">PyPI</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">croniter's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>6.2.4 (2026-07-10)</h2>\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` day-of-week low bound so\nSunday wraps correctly for stepped day-of-week ranges (``isoweekday() %\n7`` instead of ``weekday() + 1``). [44e3090,\n[#239](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239), @alhudz]\n<p>Packaging\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump pinned GitHub Actions via dependabot. [fd13d2e, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240\">#240</a>;\n5cd2e46, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238\">#238</a>]</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.2.3 (2026-07-02)</h2>\n<p>Features and Improvements</p>\n<pre><code>- Fix quadratic expansion of comma-separated range lists for\na large speed-up on expressions with many ranges. [1d79fc6,\n[#231](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/231), @alhudz]\n<p>Bugfixes</p>\n<pre><code>- Reject a zero step (e.g. ``5-5/0``) in equal and reversed\ncron ranges instead of silently accepting it. [ab27767,\n[#232](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232), @alhudz]\n- Fix ``expand_from_start_time`` month low-bound off-by-one so stepped\nmonth ranges start on the correct month. [f329964,\n[#235](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235), @alhudz]\n\nPackaging\n</code></pre>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix zizmor-reported security findings in GitHub Actions workflows.\n[ed19f94, <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/230\">#230</a>]</li>\n<li>Bump pinned build and CI dependencies via dependabot.</li>\n<li>Upgrade locked development and build dependencies (<code>uv lock\n--upgrade</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>6.2.2 (2026-03-15)</h2>\n<p>Packaging</p>\n<pre><code>- Switch build backend from ``flit_core`` to ``hatchling``\nwith pinned dependencies. [4cce160]\n- Add PEP 639 license expression (``license = &amp;quot;MIT&amp;quot;``)\nto project metadata. [4cce160]\n- Pin all GitHub Actions to SHA hashes across CI workflows. [4cce160]\n- Add dependabot for automated dependency updates. [4cce160]\n- Add zizmor workflow for CI security scanning. [4cce160]\n\n\n6.2.1 (2026-03-15)\n------------------\n\nBugfixes\n~~~~~~~~\n- Fix ``get_prev`` skipping Feb 29 on leap years for day-of-month\nexpressions. [441a0b5,\n[#203](https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/203), @Souls-R]\n\n&amp;lt;/tr&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/table&amp;gt; \n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n&lt;/blockquote&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;... (truncated)&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/details&gt;\n&lt;details&gt;\n&lt;summary&gt;Commits&lt;/summary&gt;\n\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/58534997eb4634344f00d407fb199d4d1bd057e7&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;5853499&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nPrepare for release 6.2.4 (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/241&quot;&gt;#241&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/fd13d2ec447efd854806638cb5f71a2a3a90a0b5&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fd13d2e&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/240&quot;&gt;#240&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/44e3090ae47ccf72e4027ed6fabf6a31eca42f85&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;44e3090&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nwrap sunday in expand_from_start_time day-of-week low bound (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/239&quot;&gt;#239&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/5cd2e4611e8ebea446a9d0edef3f9d8e1f30c0e3&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;5cd2e46&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/238&quot;&gt;#238&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f1eeddd7b9057b66406d162d04879258b29601d5&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;f1eeddd&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nPrepare for 6.2.4 development (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/237&quot;&gt;#237&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/22b59e05f5ca485c45596b2a9b580fddffbf753f&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;22b59e0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nPrepare for release 6.2.3 (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/236&quot;&gt;#236&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/ab277671adc8e446e8dc7f1e939eabf024b6199e&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;ab27767&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nreject zero step in equal and reversed cron ranges (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/232&quot;&gt;#232&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/f329964223eeb29e7788b1a9d615b525148fec96&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;f329964&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nfix expand_from_start_time month low bound off-by-one (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/235&quot;&gt;#235&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/9810279c20030954e2f1ed2cf5f1d34b98c6b07f&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;9810279&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nBump the github-actions group with 2 updates (&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/233&quot;&gt;#233&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/commit/d051aaf6342fbe9c559b9fcd99e6fb6f3bb63cb7&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;d051aaf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;\nBump hatchling from 1.29.0 to 1.30.1 in the pip-dependencies group\n(&lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://redirect.github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/issues/234&quot;&gt;#234&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Additional commits viewable in &lt;a\nhref=&quot;https://github.com/pallets-eco/croniter/compare/2.0.0...6.2.4&quot;&gt;compare\nview&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/details&gt;\n\n&lt;br /&gt;</code></pre>\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: erni-a <erni@caura.ai>","tree":{"sha":"719d50da57f199a1b658c61b0cbeeebbb097139e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/719d50da57f199a1b658c61b0cbeeebbb097139e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/b1657a4f2f60b42df0ff7a0b0f61a9f1a4d8e7bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqie+CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcp8QAA3bgGWE5/lY6rUs1+HOOf1B\n7eIb1VajQdtGQIqGoCJuWErcDQNtnE6igyH/Eb79N5/A9UC21