i>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.162.0...v1.163.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-genai` from 2.14.0 to 2.17.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/releases\">google-genai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.17.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.16.0...v2.17.0\">2.17.0</a>\n(2026-08-06)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add the Gemini Robotics ER 2 Preview model (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/61d4645c6f7acab5fdc1dd6a4f6943fe8c937347\">61d4645</a>)</li>\n<li>Add TOO_MANY_TOOL_CALLS to FinishReason enum. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a8ec86eab28c2806205fc8ec746b492110113c44\">a8ec86e</a>)</li>\n<li>Add top-level errors array to Interaction resource (iAPI) (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c74505b03f53e5bf54b0aed5741267f00703d218\">c74505b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add propertyOrdering auto-population for ResponseSchema and\nResponseJsonSchema for Dotnet SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3ec20812f4e6228bfa8dc766167ede2e1f925526\">3ec2081</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/80d80ffb98e95b0c62590e5593df47c74ee6e0b7\">80d80ff</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f03ecfd7734e08b60d7ea5f2123152ff1b6bdfbf\">f03ecfd</a>)</li>\n<li>Update GenerateVideos docstrings and samples (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c41ba1163f4bc7cb90d913674d1ba481d18d1248\">c41ba11</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.16.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.15.0...v2.16.0\">2.16.0</a>\n(2026-07-29)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add environment resource (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/615b6c3795f3ac005a7ed9517ddc2c86b2b7a043\">615b6c3</a>)</li>\n<li>Support GoogleMaps Tool grounding_types places and routing (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/95a335d809d75b987303d5a52e533a938585b7b5\">95a335d</a>)</li>\n<li>Wire environment service into genai sdk (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/361292ea6b5bfab276cbd6d55e7969119f9821ee\">361292e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Communicate on upcoming updates in the next major version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f63b366babf7e8549b15a7afa02c035ec78078a1\">f63b366</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.15.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7c0e1bb49a087ce1ac658ab494528379393b728a\">7c0e1bb</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.15.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.14.0...v2.15.0\">2.15.0</a>\n(2026-07-28)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/0f775f11ee7fd84433dd16252fe37698beebe296\">0f775f1</a>)</li>\n<li>Add flat <code>language_codes</code> field to\n<code>AudioTranscriptionConfig</code>. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/fc282b359a7e9e16219587266c94d2bdc506164a\">fc282b3</a>)</li>\n<li>Allow api key + proj/location for enterprise mode (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/e8714cafa739045481aedf639783f151e6a0d1e9\">e8714ca</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-genai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.16.0...v2.17.0\">2.17.0</a>\n(2026-08-06)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add the Gemini Robotics ER 2 Preview model (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/61d4645c6f7acab5fdc1dd6a4f6943fe8c937347\">61d4645</a>)</li>\n<li>Add TOO_MANY_TOOL_CALLS to FinishReason enum. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a8ec86eab28c2806205fc8ec746b492110113c44\">a8ec86e</a>)</li>\n<li>Add top-level errors array to Interaction resource (iAPI) (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c74505b03f53e5bf54b0aed5741267f00703d218\">c74505b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add propertyOrdering auto-population for ResponseSchema and\nResponseJsonSchema for Dotnet SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3ec20812f4e6228bfa8dc766167ede2e1f925526\">3ec2081</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/80d80ffb98e95b0c62590e5593df47c74ee6e0b7\">80d80ff</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f03ecfd7734e08b60d7ea5f2123152ff1b6bdfbf\">f03ecfd</a>)</li>\n<li>Update GenerateVideos docstrings and samples (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c41ba1163f4bc7cb90d913674d1ba481d18d1248\">c41ba11</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.15.0...v2.16.0\">2.16.0</a>\n(2026-07-29)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add environment resource (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/615b6c3795f3ac005a7ed9517ddc2c86b2b7a043\">615b6c3</a>)</li>\n<li>Support GoogleMaps Tool grounding_types places and routing (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/95a335d809d75b987303d5a52e533a938585b7b5\">95a335d</a>)</li>\n<li>Wire environment service into genai sdk (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/361292ea6b5bfab276cbd6d55e7969119f9821ee\">361292e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Communicate on upcoming updates in the next major version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f63b366babf7e8549b15a7afa02c035ec78078a1\">f63b366</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.15.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7c0e1bb49a087ce1ac658ab494528379393b728a\">7c0e1bb</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.14.0...v2.15.0\">2.15.0</a>\n(2026-07-28)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[GenerateContentConfig] Add\nGenerationConfig.audio_transcription_config and\nPart.audio_transcription. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/0f775f11ee7fd84433dd16252fe37698beebe296\">0f775f1</a>)</li>\n<li>Add flat <code>language_codes</code> field to\n<code>AudioTranscriptionConfig</code>. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/fc282b359a7e9e16219587266c94d2bdc506164a\">fc282b3</a>)</li>\n<li>Allow api key + proj/location for enterprise mode (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/e8714cafa739045481aedf639783f151e6a0d1e9\">e8714ca</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.14.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3d3850a2a6578603adf5ede92cba085dd9be908e\">3d3850a</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/d0efb6942142fb013c8e3217eb1c816f10f03f28\"><code>d0efb69</code></a>\nchore(main): release 2.17.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-genai/issues/2794\">#2794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3ec20812f4e6228bfa8dc766167ede2e1f925526\"><code>3ec2081</code></a>\nfix: Add propertyOrdering auto-population for ResponseSchema and\nResponseJson...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a8ec86eab28c2806205fc8ec746b492110113c44\"><code>a8ec86e</code></a>\nfeat: Add TOO_MANY_TOOL_CALLS to FinishReason enum.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a0faf87f3b88b14bb684c8fde60fc7c08c0e6d59\"><code>a0faf87</code></a>\nchore: Cleanup error dependencies</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c74505b03f53e5bf54b0aed5741267f00703d218\"><code>c74505b</code></a>\nfeat: Add top-level errors array to Interaction resource (iAPI)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/80d80ffb98e95b0c62590e5593df47c74ee6e0b7\"><code>80d80ff</code></a>\ndocs: Fix interactions</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/49b730d60e29891e4666e3035744f43f68430152\"><code>49b730d</code></a>\nchore: Cleanup deprecated field response_modalities</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/9d8301655c8628ae8dff11bd78c4c63affe70713\"><code>9d83016</code></a>\nchore: internal</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c41ba1163f4bc7cb90d913674d1ba481d18d1248\"><code>c41ba11</code></a>\ndocs: Update GenerateVideos docstrings and samples</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/9a2f8cb76e747a6c72941c8069ed956e82f3431c\"><code>9a2f8cb</code></a>\nrefactor: delete deprecated StreamMetadata proto field and message\ndefinition</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.14.0...v2.17.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `openai` from 2.48.0 to 2.53.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/releases\">openai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.53.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.52.1...v2.53.0\">2.53.0</a>\n(2026-08-03)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> Add gpt-5.5 and tool name/namespace to\nResponses types (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3569\">#3569</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/dd1202d5dacff985861289c1d9c46996ded2d2a5\">dd1202d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ci:</strong> avoid NumPy source builds and duplicate HTTPX\ncoverage (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3573\">#3573</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/b58332f8a0717f7b1effb1788a594011cee6e02f\">b58332f</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.52.1</h2>\n<h2>2.52.1 (2026-07-31)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.52.0...v2.52.1\">v2.52.0...v2.52.1</a></p>\n<h3>Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ci:</strong> pin setup-uv v5 to its underlying commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3560\">#3560</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/cbdc98b6c1e21df7ee43d13b5de7243c6ed1ee7f\">cbdc98b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.52.0</h2>\n<h2>2.52.0 (2026-07-31)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.51.0...v2.52.0\">v2.51.0...v2.52.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> content provenance checks (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1d6c1180f8eaa71bfd45cae67360987b2bea3656\">1d6c118</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> honor Retry-After delays up to two minutes\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3555\">#3555</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7fa7946485b5ecbadd0ebf8624c574e2c9e3370c\">7fa7946</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>add API-key mTLS HTTP client recipes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3552\">#3552</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7a3d5e46b61cb36109dc4e7fd6d4ab70cc6d6c0f\">7a3d5e4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.51.0</h2>\n<h2>2.51.0 (2026-07-30)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.50.0...v2.51.0\">v2.50.0...v2.51.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> fast tier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/8808ed27952dae13fb8761f045376af5b3e5bec2\">8808ed2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">openai's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.52.1...v2.53.0\">2.53.0</a>\n(2026-08-03)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> Add gpt-5.5 and tool name/namespace to\nResponses types (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3569\">#3569</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/dd1202d5dacff985861289c1d9c46996ded2d2a5\">dd1202d</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ci:</strong> avoid NumPy source builds and duplicate HTTPX\ncoverage (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3573\">#3573</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/b58332f8a0717f7b1effb1788a594011cee6e02f\">b58332f</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.52.1 (2026-07-31)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.52.0...v2.52.1\">v2.52.0...v2.52.1</a></p>\n<h3>Chores</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>ci:</strong> pin setup-uv v5 to its underlying commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3560\">#3560</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/cbdc98b6c1e21df7ee43d13b5de7243c6ed1ee7f\">cbdc98b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.52.0 (2026-07-31)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.51.0...v2.52.0\">v2.51.0...v2.52.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> content provenance checks (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/1d6c1180f8eaa71bfd45cae67360987b2bea3656\">1d6c118</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>client:</strong> honor Retry-After delays up to two minutes\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3555\">#3555</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7fa7946485b5ecbadd0ebf8624c574e2c9e3370c\">7fa7946</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>add API-key mTLS HTTP client recipes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3552\">#3552</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7a3d5e46b61cb36109dc4e7fd6d4ab70cc6d6c0f\">7a3d5e4</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.51.0 (2026-07-30)</h2>\n<p>Full Changelog: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.50.0...v2.51.0\">v2.50.0...v2.51.0</a></p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> fast tier (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/8808ed27952dae13fb8761f045376af5b3e5bec2\">8808ed2</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>api:</strong> add fast tier to helper methods (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/60641266ff4b296044a81fe1717c17a70ceadbf1\">6064126</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/5e36cd326fa2ebe00260386e7a27fe1c8c02d4fd\"><code>5e36cd3</code></a>\nrelease: 2.53.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3575\">#3575</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/875a5c21353f43e6a4c3810c1cbaf56980f27f7b\"><code>875a5c2</code></a>\nci: prepare checks for merge queue (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3574\">#3574</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/b58332f8a0717f7b1effb1788a594011cee6e02f\"><code>b58332f</code></a>\nfix(ci): avoid NumPy source builds and duplicate HTTPX coverage (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3573\">#3573</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/dd1202d5dacff985861289c1d9c46996ded2d2a5\"><code>dd1202d</code></a>\nfeat(api): Add gpt-5.5 and tool name/namespace to Responses types (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3569\">#3569</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/24b7cd19ced5aa4e402558bc3f1fbc67abb33134\"><code>24b7cd1</code></a>\nci: migrate release-please to upstream action (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3568\">#3568</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/f83b1f4cce7f25a11079341e28a76f71b1d6b2fb\"><code>f83b1f4</code></a>\nrelease: 2.52.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3562\">#3562</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/cbdc98b6c1e21df7ee43d13b5de7243c6ed1ee7f\"><code>cbdc98b</code></a>\nchore(ci): pin setup-uv v5 to its underlying commit (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3560\">#3560</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/ca693fbaa20a620ce53a48f4419a1a01444564e7\"><code>ca693fb</code></a>\nrelease: 2.52.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/2ad8c98747a0cbf9abd7c5a6bc8f74186e57fb6f\"><code>2ad8c98</code></a>\nfeat(api): content provenance checks</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/commit/7a3d5e46b61cb36109dc4e7fd6d4ab70cc6d6c0f\"><code>7a3d5e4</code></a>\ndocs: add API-key mTLS HTTP client recipes (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/openai/openai-python/issues/3552\">#3552</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/openai/openai-python/compare/v2.48.0...v2.53.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cachetools` from 7.1.6 to 7.1.7\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/blob/master/CHANGELOG.rst\">cachetools's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>v7.1.7 (2026-08-01)</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Improve <code>Cache.__setitem__</code> behavior when replacing an\nexisting\ncache item with a larger value.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Update CI environment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/01af8e5b7ce44432b357e26c7d67eb7fa055ae72\"><code>01af8e5</code></a>\nRelease v7.1.7.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/ccaa8c8c882b7cb76904ea5ae21aae33cca0c2c1\"><code>ccaa8c8</code></a>\nMinor stylistic improvements.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/c65b625da6a0e73839100a0d5f5153b4245d1689\"><code>c65b625</code></a>\nPrepare v7.1.7.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/89a5928c2f8abee030c34e7964523872cb2a81ba\"><code>89a5928</code></a>\nBump actions/setup-python from 6.3.0 to 7.0.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/411\">#411</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/39b31bc9b63abe98497409945e9d382d8918c8fb\"><code>39b31bc</code></a>\nFix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/405\">#405</a>:\nFix Cache.<strong>setitem</strong> over-evicting when growing an\nexisting key</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/commit/16e88894ef7d79b25a68f5a3b5411ed881342725\"><code>16e8889</code></a>\nBump actions/checkout from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/tkem/cachetools/issues/410\">#410</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tkem/cachetools/compare/v7.1.6...v7.1.7\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-cloud-pubsub` from 2.39.0 to 2.39.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/releases\">google-cloud-pubsub's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>google-cloud-pubsub: v2.39.1</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-cloud-pubsub-v2.39.0...google-cloud-pubsub-v2.39.1\">2.39.1</a>\n(2026-08-06)</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>bump grpcio to 1.59.0; require Python 3.10+ (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17351\">#17351</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/a53487a009c21912ea6c99fe3a5e0e52a26b31ef\">a53487a</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/905bfe39396d0062fde6df462e5c495e93b9749e\"><code>905bfe3</code></a>\nchore: release main (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17832\">#17832</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/ad8f93c3211b3ae9d9b234a5b2fa52a8cbf4b206\"><code>ad8f93c</code></a>\nfix(api-core): use truthiness check in setup_request_id to support\nproto-plus...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/06dd2c00e6ca3f7d174cc03cb4dba9371bf1ff47\"><code>06dd2c0</code></a>\nchore: bump google-api-core to 2.28.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18003\">#18003</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/08f21a6bfc357d249a6c85cd9d4282154fa9aba2\"><code>08f21a6</code></a>\nfix(proto-plus): add context to TypeErrors during message manipulation\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17682\">#17682</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/32fd4796a6c47b1cad4c9f2881913da51fda2adf\"><code>32fd479</code></a>\ntests(spanner): avoid table name collisions in tests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/18001\">#18001</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/2207ca66fe9b5d5aff201dd922f37df06ab4b664\"><code>2207ca6</code></a>\nfeat: add pandas-gbq capability helper (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17957\">#17957</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/6167e4136e24a40fa6fc77be5987ba9cab8ac5e8\"><code>6167e41</code></a>\nfix: deduplicate x-goog-api-client headers (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17616\">#17616</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/71bc6223ee0f344b2bc91ddcab82ab0b1b8fc19b\"><code>71bc622</code></a>\ndocs: add connector libraries overview table to package README (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17939\">#17939</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/1b5c48b851d92d77f9fb4ce5beea57a22281445d\"><code>1b5c48b</code></a>\nfix(bigframes): fix field name typos for ai.generate* functions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17983\">#17983</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/commit/f64ada29ff596202a5625f71516f0215e45aa8ae\"><code>f64ada2</code></a>\nfix: avoid retaining routing parameter instances in cache (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/issues/17961\">#17961</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python/compare/google-cloud-pubsub-v2.39.0...google-cloud-pubsub-v2.39.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ddtrace` from 4.11.1 to 4.12.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/releases\">ddtrace's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>4.12.2</h2>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>aws_durable_execution_sdk_python: This fix resolves an issue where a\nreplayed durable operation that had failed permanently reported an\nincorrect <code>aws.durable.replayed</code> value and an\n<code>aws.durable.operation_attempt</code> one higher than its original\nexecution.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.12.1</h2>\n<h2>Bug Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>CI Visibility: This fix resolves an issue where the Datadog UI showed\n<code>No extra information available</code> when viewing details about\nwhy a test was\nskipped by Intelligent Test Runner, due to missing ITR correlation ID on\ntest or suite events.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Code Security (IAST): fixes an issue where taint tracking could abort\nthe Python process when old-style <code>%</code> string formatting\nhandled tainted<br />\ntext containing literal IAST evidence marker delimiters.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Code Security (IAST): This fix scopes\n<code>copy_ranges_from_strings</code> and\n<code>copy_and_shift_ranges_from_strings</code> to the active request\nslot, matching<br />\nthe scoped taint read path. Previously these copy helpers resolved the\ntaint map by scanning all request slots, so a concurrent or\nstill-open<br />\nrequest could capture the derived taint and the current request would\nmiss the transformed tainted input.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>LLM Observability: Resolves a <code>TypeError</code> raised during\nstreamed tool-call reconstruction when an OpenAI-compatible backend\n(e.g.<br />\nDashScope/Qwen) emits a tool-call delta with\n<code>function.arguments</code> or <code>custom.input</code> set to\n<code>None</code> instead of <code>&quot;&quot;</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix crashes in uwsgi worker when exiting from SIGTERM.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>IAST: A crash occurring when using <code>uvloop</code> has been\nfixed.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>LLM Observability: Resolves an issue where the OpenAI and LiteLLM\nintegrations reported zero cost for OpenRouter requests using a<br />\nbring-your-own-key setup.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4.12.0</h2>\n<h3>Upgrade Notes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>LLM Observability:\n<ul>\n<li>When APM and LLMObs are both enabled, the APM trace writer now uses\nthe <code>v0.4</code> trace API version (<code>v0.5</code> cannot carry\nthe LLMObs span data). Setting <code>DD_TRACE_API_VERSION=v0.5</code>\nwith LLMObs enabled logs a warning and downgrades to <code>v0.4</code>.\nNo user action is required.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<ul>\n<li>ASM:\n<ul>\n<li>This upgrades libddwaf to 2.0.0.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>New Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>AI Guard:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add AI Guard support for LangChain 1.0+ agents built with\n<code>create_agent</code>.</li>\n<li>This introduces the <code>DD_AI_GUARD_OPENAI_ENABLED</code>\nenvironment variable (<code>true</code> by default) as a per-provider\nkill switch. Set it to <code>false</code> to disable AI Guard\nauto-instrumentation of the OpenAI SDK without affecting other providers\nor requiring a tracer version rollback.</li>\n<li>Added opt-in evaluation of streamed OpenAI Chat Completions and\nResponses via <code>DD_AI_GUARD_ANALYZE_STREAM_RESPONSES_ENABLED</code>\n(default off); streams are buffered and evaluated before any chunk is\ndelivered, raising <code>AIGuardAbortError</code> on a block.</li>\n<li>This introduces AI Guard standalone mode. When APM tracing is\ndisabled (<code>DD_APM_TRACING_ENABLED=false</code>), traces produced by\nAI Guard are still sent to Datadog, kept with <code>USER_KEEP</code>\nsampling priority and the AI Guard decision maker so that they can be\nattributed to AI Guard, while APM host billing is not triggered.</li>\n<li>Add opt-in buffered stream response evaluation for AI Guard on\nAnthropic streaming calls. When\n<code>DD_AI_GUARD_ANALYZE_STREAM_RESPONSES_ENABLED=true</code> (default\n<code>false</code>), all streamed chunks are buffered, the full\nassistant response is evaluated by AI Guard, and chunks are replayed to\nthe caller only after an ALLOW verdict. On DENY/ABORT,\n<code>AIGuardAbortError</code> is raised and zero chunks are delivered.\nWhen the flag is off (the default), streaming behavior is\nunchanged.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>AAP:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Adds the normalized HTTP route span tag\n(<code>_dd.appsec.normalized_route</code>) for Tornado, following\nRFC-1103 and the existing FastAPI, Starlette, Django, and Flask\nimplementations. The tag is emitted on every request span that already\ncarries <code>http.route</code> when the API Security feature is active.\nTornado routes using named capturing groups\n(<code>(?P&lt;name&gt;...)</code>) produce named parameters (e.g.\n<code>/users/{id}</code>); positional groups produce auto-numbered\nplaceholders (e.g. <code>{param1}</code>). Optional trailing-slash\npatterns (<code>/?</code>) are treated as not declaring a trailing slash\nper RFC-1103 rule 1. <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/18398\">#18398</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/69ecf2dc78bcc1aa5ed05e935ff0038f2293c1da\"><code>69ecf2d</code></a>\nfix(aws_durable_execution_sdk_python): [SVLS-9168] handle FAILED\ncheckpoints ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/f1b2b874e250dace1d7e36613c6eea0caa88aea1\"><code>f1b2b87</code></a>\nchore: bump version to 4.12.2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19413\">#19413</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/ddb76086b5caa94fc6fcd8d46c890fffabd62018\"><code>ddb7608</code></a>\nchore(version): set version to 4.12.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19392\">#19392</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/7599b6da0f2339597925f802197ae0815eb781ff\"><code>7599b6d</code></a>\nchore: raise RSS SLO for tracing-profiling-enabled scenario [backport\n4.12] (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/e20e14bf92d8098dab47aae543844b154e4c7679\"><code>e20e14b</code></a>\nfix(llmobs): coerce None tool-call arguments in openai streamed chunk\nreconst...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/31503e230dafb7e8cd918f2e806f7d0fe21f8f86\"><code>31503e2</code></a>\nfix(llmobs): surface OpenRouter BYOK upstream cost [backport 4.12] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19367\">#19367</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/845f8cf916734e313c0488f3405021019465a4ab\"><code>845f8cf</code></a>\nfix(native): run shutdown in thread in uwsgi [backport 4.12] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19345\">#19345</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/02989372a12d75d9cf37dc331b9e1171ec27f054\"><code>0298937</code></a>\nfix(iast): handle literal evidence markers in modulo propagation\n[backport 4....</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/361a9faa2ce6e1b92f857544b6fbffcbe3710aae\"><code>361a9fa</code></a>\nchore(iast): preserve propagation during source suppression [backport\n4.12] (...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/commit/357169a7e49799fc90a033a5c32dc9440c652cb7\"><code>357169a</code></a>\nfix(ci_visibility): add ITR correlation ID [backport 4.12] (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/issues/19241\">#19241</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/compare/v4.11.1...v4.12.2\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.16.0 to 0.16.2\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases\">ruff's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.16.2</h2>\n<h2>Release Notes</h2>\n<p>Released on 2026-08-06.</p>\n<h3>Bug fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>[<code>flake8-pyi</code>] Avoid false positives on\n<code>singledispatch</code> functions (<code>PYI041</code>) (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27335\">#27335</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Server</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Register formatting capabilities dynamically to exclude TOML files\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/astral-sh/ruff/pull/27332\">#27332</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/MeGaGiGaGon\"><code>@​MeGaGiGaGon</code></a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/charliermarsh\"><code>@​charliermarsh</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/epage\"><code>@​epage</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sharkdp\"><code>@​sharkdp</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ntBre\"><code>@​ntBre</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Install ruff 0.16.2</h2>\n<h3>Install prebuilt binaries via shell script</h3>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf\nhttps://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-installer.sh\n| sh\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Install prebuilt binaries via powershell script</h3>\n<pre lang=\"sh\"><code>powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -c &quot;irm\nhttps://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-installer.ps1\n| iex&quot;\n</code></pre>\n<h2>Download ruff 0.16.2</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Platform</th>\n<th>Checksum</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz\">ruff-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>Apple Silicon macOS</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz\">ruff-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>Intel macOS</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.zip\">ruff-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.zip</a></td>\n<td>ARM64 Windows</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-i686-pc-windows-msvc.zip\">ruff-i686-pc-windows-msvc.zip</a></td>\n<td>x86 Windows</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-i686-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip\">ruff-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip</a></td>\n<td>x64 Windows</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz\">ruff-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>ARM64 Linux</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-i686-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz\">ruff-i686-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>x86 Linux</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-i686-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz.sha256\">checksum</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruff/releases/download/0.16.2/ruff-powerpc64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz\">ruff-powerpc64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz</a></td>\n<td>PPC64 Linux</td>\n<td><a\nhref=\"https://releases.astral.sh/github/ruf…","tree":{"sha":"2f5b45fc6495e1aa5614fd58ed0def78e9a3e323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/trees/2f5b45fc6495e1aa5614fd58ed0def78e9a3e323"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/caura-ai/caura/git/commits/a72a5d3b251735eb2a91c3036577fb80bf5bdcd8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfg3ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMzwQADHyKMnWIYNiXiB7tw/pCg+d\n1Jw+riLZzVgoRHumSuhHCJSKFaiPFY7Q4PEs20IIppvv1Nm186n5T/Tz1mBBU2lW\ndKvwqkq5zgrLqMgN8bcrBfV91FVxJjhl/A4iD4TAHxvdj3sQiGmGh5Y1MZ6NF9AF\nR+Qaq3HQ6HoH5X7htfl/d3Rq+vYy9JMgzYjVdpmReXIJyBD6zJetIHvKLbGCufmh\nCbZK/WjOUrOOXJ99Ei/TA1okwzWh38Tep6U5fxLljTFWuNPS0yNTW94vtFt0/cNP\nJOtjEfPhjcNKI2xsbfSNs3pNp0CVkyftJyOeg+GQNbzzErHzLRNxYLclnK2NAm4Z\nC8CkCsfzmRBJL9rWZog6HAchXl1qAWuPJiJIxN+fe8efpBYwO3yQtrzwLqg7jND4\n+yp0X3rLJF4OFeR9Ddgsr2kWyxs+5UaQBYCyJfmL7UyALtPHomKgsBJjjE3lcfvU\ndgUWPFeGYfN5u6hSYrRGAtT9L6fLGvKPE4KVToW5Nol3koDZcQdqOGdytGEAB19R\nvNV5eP+XUuKKc7DQuwANeBqrxGKbYJr3jBITMZcNi8mSrdzJaSAAly57aIQQp6gA\nW9SoYPdFPdUK2Od1hv+IIt92aaLQNs1IUeXVDRv8iIRyE3iub4gG2Onp2bDvB7T7\nKr8gwP4FaMwC+UY5Ri5D\n=SNkl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2f5b45fc6495e1aa5614fd58ed0def78e9a3e323\nparent 936238fcce600bb6b931698ce099d8893a00bd5b\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786645960 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786645960 +0300\n\ndeps: bump the uv-minor-patch group across 4 directories with 11 updates (#747)\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 10 updates in the /core-api\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.140.0` | `0.141.1`\n|\n| [alembic](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic) | `1.18.5` | `1.19.0`\n|\n| [pydantic-settings](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings) |\n`2.14.2` | `2.15.0` |\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.162.0` | `1.163.0` |\n| [google-genai](https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai) | `2.14.0`\n| `2.17.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.48.0` |\n`2.53.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.6` | `7.1.7` |\n|\n[google-cloud-pubsub](https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)\n| `2.39.0` | `2.39.1` |\n| [ddtrace](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py) | `4.11.1` |\n`4.12.2` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.16.0` | `0.16.2` |\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /core-operations\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.140.0` | `0.141.1`\n|\n| [pydantic-settings](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings) |\n`2.14.2` | `2.15.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.6` | `7.1.7` |\n|\n[google-cloud-pubsub](https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)\n| `2.39.0` | `2.39.1` |\n| [ddtrace](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py) | `4.11.1` |\n`4.12.2` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.16.0` | `0.16.2` |\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 7 updates in the /core-storage-api\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.140.0` | `0.141.1`\n|\n| [alembic](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic) | `1.18.5` | `1.19.0`\n|\n| [pydantic-settings](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings) |\n`2.14.2` | `2.15.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.48.0` |\n`2.53.0` |\n|\n[google-cloud-pubsub](https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)\n| `2.39.0` | `2.39.1` |\n| [ddtrace](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py) | `4.11.1` |\n`4.12.2` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.16.0` | `0.16.2` |\n\nBumps the uv-minor-patch group with 9 updates in the /core-worker\ndirectory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [fastapi](https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) | `0.140.0` | `0.141.1`\n|\n| [pydantic-settings](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings) |\n`2.14.2` | `2.15.0` |\n|\n[google-cloud-aiplatform](https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform)\n| `1.162.0` | `1.163.0` |\n| [openai](https://github.com/openai/openai-python) | `2.48.0` |\n`2.53.0` |\n| [cachetools](https://github.com/tkem/cachetools) | `7.1.6` | `7.1.7` |\n|\n[google-cloud-pubsub](https://github.com/googleapis/google-cloud-python)\n| `2.39.0` | `2.39.1` |\n| [ddtrace](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py) | `4.11.1` |\n`4.12.2` |\n| [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) | `0.16.0` | `0.16.2` |\n|\n[sentence-transformers](https://github.com/huggingface/sentence-transformers)\n| `5.6.1` | `5.7.0` |\n\n\nUpdates `fastapi` from 0.140.0 to 0.141.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases\">fastapi's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.141.1</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix support for background tasks and headers from dependencies in\n<code>app.frontend()</code>. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16105\">#16105</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Document <code>FASTAPI_ENV</code> in FastAPI CLI guide. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16104\">#16104</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.141.0</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>✨ Add <code>app.frontend(check_dir=&quot;auto&quot;)</code>, to make\nlocal development more convenient with <code>fastapi dev</code>. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16102\">#16102</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.140.13</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix <code>status_code</code> being ignored for SSE and JSONL\nstreaming endpoints. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15937\">#15937</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SAURABHSALVE\"><code>@​SAURABHSALVE</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>📝 Fix <code>format_sse_event</code> docstring rendering of\n<code>\\n\\n</code> terminator. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15613\">#15613</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/AshNicolus\"><code>@​AshNicolus</code></a>.</li>\n<li>📝 Add API reference page for fastapi.sse. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15930\">#15930</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/SAURABHSALVE\"><code>@​SAURABHSALVE</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.140.12</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix line splitting in <code>format_sse_event</code> to comply with\nSSE spec. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15515\">#15515</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Zawwarsami16\"><code>@​Zawwarsami16</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.140.11</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix <code>response_model_*</code> params ignored for non-generator\nendpoints with <code>Iterable[..]</code> return type. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/15093\">#15093</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.140.10</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix handling sequences with nested Annotated types. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/14874\">#14874</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/YuriiMotov\"><code>@​YuriiMotov</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Internal</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Accept any base test failure as regression. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16092\">#16092</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>🐛 Preserve pytest exit code in regression check. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16091\">#16091</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n<li>✅ Test PR regressions against base code. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16090\">#16090</a>\nby <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/tiangolo\"><code>@​tiangolo</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.140.9</h2>\n<h3>Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>🐛 Fix <code>exclude_defaults</code> not propagated to dict keys and\nvalues in <code>jsonable_encoder</code>. PR <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16043\">#16043</a>\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/MBGrao\"><code>@​MBGrao</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/95f8322ee1dcda7ceace7b1c4f6c9915b36d748f\"><code>95f8322</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.141.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16106\">#16106</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/f137944c435cff4e4b30ea7d12855ea88ddb868c\"><code>f137944</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/d62354434b2e508fe89024213b220ca8e67dea5e\"><code>d623544</code></a>\n🐛 Fix support for background tasks and headers from dependencies in\n`app.fron...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/1d211b9c1009d577f39fa2b19b10d9a93a72a0ed\"><code>1d211b9</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/8a1f8768411e62093e70ce142ea10863a485643c\"><code>8a1f876</code></a>\n📝 Document <code>FASTAPI_ENV</code> in FastAPI CLI guide (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16104\">#16104</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/c7e7b651d6946c07cc9f675f39c9501d08319e57\"><code>c7e7b65</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.141.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16103\">#16103</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/6bceb84053eb2405e9c000aad30ea13367b5ee32\"><code>6bceb84</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/5429fed84e84e32672c25a953eca3429b841ce90\"><code>5429fed</code></a>\n✨ Add <code>app.frontend(check_dir=&quot;auto&quot;)</code>, to make\nlocal development more conven...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/628663f4f899c465da423bce681c7adf9a218948\"><code>628663f</code></a>\n🔖 Release version 0.140.13 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/16096\">#16096</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/commit/0b54fd00273019034dd30b120ac842e65d80690e\"><code>0b54fd0</code></a>\n📝 Update release notes</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/compare/0.140.0...0.141.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `alembic` from 1.18.5 to 1.19.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/releases\">alembic's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>1.19.0</h1>\n<p>Released: August 4, 2026</p>\n<h2>changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[changed] [installation]</strong> Environmental updates:</p>\n<pre><code>- Trove classifiers now include Python 3.15 which is now part\nof CI\n    integration\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Python 3.14 is also added to trove classifiers which had been\npreviously\nomitted</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Implemented <a href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0604\">PEP 604</a>\nstyle unions in type annotations\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>feature</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[feature] [autogenerate]</strong> Autogenerate now detects\nthe addition and removal of named CHECK\nconstraints, as part of the default autogenerate behavior. Detection is\nname-based only; a constraint whose name is unchanged is presumed\nequivalent regardless of its expression text, as reliably normalizing\nSQL expressions across backends for comparison purposes is not generally\nfeasible. This behavior is implemented as a plugin named\n<code>alembic.autogenerate.checkconstraint_byname</code>, and may be\ndisabled if not\ndesired by excluding it from the\n<code>EnvironmentContext.configure.autogenerate_plugins</code> list.\nPull request courtesy Francois van Kempen.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/508\">#508</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>bug</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>[bug] [commands]</strong> Fixed inconsistency where running\n<code>stamp</code> or <code>downgrade</code> to <code>base</code> in\noffline (<code>--sql</code>) mode would emit a <code>DROP TABLE\nalembic_version</code>\nstatement, while the same operations in online mode never drop the\nversion\ntable. Offline mode no longer emits this <code>DROP</code>, matching\nonline\nbehavior. The version table continues to be created when it does not\nexist;\nonly the spurious offline-only drop has been removed.  Pull request\ncourtesy imurodl.</p>\n<p>References: <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/issues/1822\">#1822</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic/commits\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `pydantic-settings` from 2.14.2 to 2.15.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/releases\">pydantic-settings's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.15.0</h2>\n<h2>Highlights</h2>\n<h3>Behavior changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><code>case_sensitive</code> now applies to init kwargs and\nconfig-file sources</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/900\">#900</a>).\n<code>InitSettingsSource</code> and the JSON/TOML/YAML config sources\npreviously ignored <code>case_sensitive</code>. Since it defaults to\n<code>False</code>, <strong>case-insensitive matching is now the\ndefault</strong> for these sources — e.g.\n<code>Settings(TeSt=...)</code> now populates a <code>test</code> field\nwhere it previously did not. Nested keys are still matched\ncase-sensitively.</li>\n<li><strong>Fields with unresolved forward references now emit a\nwarning</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/901\">#901</a>).\nSettings sources can silently fail to resolve such fields; they now\nraise <code>IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning</code> telling you to call\n<code>model_rebuild()</code>. If you have <code>filterwarnings =\nerror</code> configured, this may surface as a new failure.</li>\n<li><strong>Non-JSON env values for strict fields now raise\n<code>ValidationError</code></strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/926\">#926</a>)\ninstead of a less specific error.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>New features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Show environment variable names in CLI help</strong> via\n<code>cli_show_env_vars=True</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/860\">#860</a>),\nso generated <code>--help</code> output doubles as configuration\ndocumentation.</li>\n<li><strong><code>PYDANTIC_SETTINGS_DEBUG</code> for debugging settings\nresolution</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/906\">#906</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/913\">#913</a>).\nSet it to a truthy value with <code>DEBUG</code> logging enabled to see\neach source's contribution in priority order, which source won for each\nvalue, and which <code>env_file</code>/secret files were probed, loaded,\nor skipped — the long-standing &quot;why isn't my <code>.env</code>\nbeing picked up?&quot; question.</li>\n<li><strong><code>toml_table_header</code> for regular TOML\nfiles</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/882\">#882</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/886\">#886</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/887\">#887</a>),\nletting you root settings at a nested table in any TOML file, not just\n<code>pyproject.toml</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>Traversable</code> support for JSON/TOML/YAML file\nsources</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/902\">#902</a>),\nso you can load config packaged inside a distribution — including files\ninside a zip or wheel — via <code>importlib.resources.files(...)</code>\nwithout casting to <code>Path</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>GCP: <code>project_id</code> can come from an earlier\nsettings source</strong> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/878\">#878</a>),\nrather than only from the constructor or\n<code>GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix env vars not loading on Windows with\n<code>case_sensitive=True</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/894\">#894</a>).\nWindows upper-cases <code>os.environ</code> keys, so fields raised\n<code>Field required</code> instead of picking up their values.</li>\n<li>Read secret files as UTF-8 instead of the platform locale encoding\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/917\">#917</a>).\nOn Windows code pages such as cp1252 this silently corrupted non-ASCII\nsecrets.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>AliasPath</code> on nested model fields not JSON-decoding\nenv values (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/898\">#898</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix case-insensitive matching for <strong>optional</strong> nested\nmodels (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/905\">#905</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix dotenv extras being wrongly claimed by a complex field sharing a\nname prefix (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/912\">#912</a>)\n— e.g. <code>dbx_token</code> being swallowed by a <code>db: dict</code>\nfield.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>nested_model_default_partial_update=True</code> corrupting\ndiscriminated unions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/876\">#876</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix <code>Secret</code> subclasses crashing when loaded from the\nenvironment (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/920\">#920</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix enum names not parsing through nested annotations such as\n<code>Optional[Annotated[MyEnum, ...]]</code> with\n<code>env_parse_enums=True</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/910\">#910</a>).</li>\n<li>An empty <code>yaml_config_section</code> now falls back to defaults\ninstead of raising <code>AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no\nattribute 'keys'</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/914\">#914</a>).</li>\n<li><code>NestedSecretsSettingsSource</code> no longer follows symlinks\npointing outside <code>secrets_dir</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/889\">#889</a>).</li>\n<li>GCP: skip the <code>list_secrets</code> call when\n<code>case_sensitive=True</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/862\">#862</a>),\nlowering the required IAM permissions to just\n<code>roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor</code>.</li>\n<li>AWS: <code>types-boto3[secretsmanager]</code> is no longer required\nat runtime (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/880\">#880</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Document JSON parsing of complex env values, plus a\ncomma-separated-values recipe (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/919\">#919</a>).</li>\n<li>Recommend an async settings loading pattern (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/908\">#908</a>).</li>\n<li>Clarify behavior when an unprefixed value is present in a dotenv\nfile (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/895\">#895</a>).</li>\n<li>Clarify environment variable helper descriptions (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/867\">#867</a>)\nand fix assorted typos (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/904\">#904</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update documentation link for Pydantic settings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/hramezani\"><code>@​hramezani</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/863\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#863</a></li>\n<li>Bump the python-packages group with 4 updates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/865\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#865</a></li>\n<li>docs: clarify environment variable helper descriptions by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vip892766gma\"><code>@​vip892766gma</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/867\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#867</a></li>\n<li>Bump the python-packages group with 4 updates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/870\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#870</a></li>\n<li>Bump the python-packages group with 4 updates by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/875\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#875</a></li>\n<li>Skip list_secrets call when case_sensitive=True by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ecerulm\"><code>@​ecerulm</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/862\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#862</a></li>\n<li>GoogleSecretManagerSettingsSource: read project_id from previous\nsources by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ecerulm\"><code>@​ecerulm</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/pull/878\">pydantic/pydantic-settings#878</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/f725ca187bee4212e9ef799eefa3cb25be788462\"><code>f725ca1</code></a>\nPrepare release 2.15.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/930\">#930</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/28f35c25fac5d61210d532c31a300d49c0b684a4\"><code>28f35c2</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 4 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/929\">#929</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/9056db049560897229f2603493753bae27b6479f\"><code>9056db0</code></a>\ntest: move function-local imports to the top of test modules (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/927\">#927</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/f077e3ab3d9492838c7ef9275a88c95134688095\"><code>f077e3a</code></a>\nfix: raise ValidationError for non-JSON env values on strict fields (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/926\">#926</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/ae25d703c458b57f5a9a425f6ec9a28ad868f980\"><code>ae25d70</code></a>\nfix: treat Secret subclasses as non-complex fields (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/716\">#716</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/920\">#920</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/798dcea2a23b08a3e9b37994014e036224f6dd18\"><code>798dcea</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 4 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/924\">#924</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/a190041d353bda2d432ea1908de4c499ae89ee0a\"><code>a190041</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 4 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/925\">#925</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/5d9333282b5c85d65a457c45e4476369b9949726\"><code>5d93332</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 4 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/921\">#921</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/d2fdeda91157140d2ff0c05404f32a9b1218115a\"><code>d2fdeda</code></a>\nfix: read secret files as UTF-8 instead of the locale encoding (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/917\">#917</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/commit/2256a4e60f83f2da81e7654252562fc4841aa5d4\"><code>2256a4e</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/issues/915\">#915</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-settings/compare/v2.14.2...v2.15.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-cloud-aiplatform` from 1.162.0 to 1.163.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/releases\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.163.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.162.0...v1.163.0\">1.163.0</a>\n(2026-07-28)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add create EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/07ade2e2384a6bd58b8de6b6e59647fda0d81b97\">07ade2e</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add delete/update EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/09e5a65c233770fcf2b1cdbe31ead775e2395d02\">09e5a65</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add get/list EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/52b1c24f5db291a190b5e1023d2128a700a36c71\">52b1c24</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nexport_open_model support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c2ba5d247991986d71094c41e418704865b55fa0\">c2ba5d2</a>)</li>\n<li>Support us mREP endpoint for Batch Prediction, Training, and Online\nPrediction. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/96a9fcf5bb0aca0e42f39428a041d0c70f7f9bc3\">96a9fcf</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Depend on the <code>autogen</code> distribution instead of\n<code>ag2</code> for the AG2 integration. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/dbcf815680812e1beee23e15c20f12a435ace47b\">dbcf815</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Resolve opentelemetry-resourcedetector-gcp dependency\nerror (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a16fc0df5472fc0ca6f063bb0b3c4cdb2995c131\">a16fc0d</a>)</li>\n<li>Merge sandbox-only turns in SDK-side interaction-to-AgentData\nconversion. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f93c45555512a3f3f27441194cbc8383b36fc358\">f93c455</a>)</li>\n<li>Send display_name when creating a sandbox environment template. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/243ca19c2b71c2fe1be727cba878ae7e6703eae3\">243ca19</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">google-cloud-aiplatform's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.162.0...v1.163.0\">1.163.0</a>\n(2026-07-28)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add create EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/07ade2e2384a6bd58b8de6b6e59647fda0d81b97\">07ade2e</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add delete/update EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/09e5a65c233770fcf2b1cdbe31ead775e2395d02\">09e5a65</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI Client(evals) - add get/list EvaluationExperiment (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/52b1c24f5db291a190b5e1023d2128a700a36c71\">52b1c24</a>)</li>\n<li>Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nexport_open_model support (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c2ba5d247991986d71094c41e418704865b55fa0\">c2ba5d2</a>)</li>\n<li>Support us mREP endpoint for Batch Prediction, Training, and Online\nPrediction. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/96a9fcf5bb0aca0e42f39428a041d0c70f7f9bc3\">96a9fcf</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Depend on the <code>autogen</code> distribution instead of\n<code>ag2</code> for the AG2 integration. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/dbcf815680812e1beee23e15c20f12a435ace47b\">dbcf815</a>)</li>\n<li>GenAI client - Resolve opentelemetry-resourcedetector-gcp dependency\nerror (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a16fc0df5472fc0ca6f063bb0b3c4cdb2995c131\">a16fc0d</a>)</li>\n<li>Merge sandbox-only turns in SDK-side interaction-to-AgentData\nconversion. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f93c45555512a3f3f27441194cbc8383b36fc358\">f93c455</a>)</li>\n<li>Send display_name when creating a sandbox environment template. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/243ca19c2b71c2fe1be727cba878ae7e6703eae3\">243ca19</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/6845eaf9c5513198f6eba11d2c091a4a29c35565\"><code>6845eaf</code></a>\nchore(main): release 1.163.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/issues/7017\">#7017</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/09e5a65c233770fcf2b1cdbe31ead775e2395d02\"><code>09e5a65</code></a>\nfeat: GenAI Client(evals) - add delete/update EvaluationExperiment</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/c2ba5d247991986d71094c41e418704865b55fa0\"><code>c2ba5d2</code></a>\nfeat: Onboard Vertex Model Garden to GenAI Python SDK: Add\nexport_open_model ...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/96a9fcf5bb0aca0e42f39428a041d0c70f7f9bc3\"><code>96a9fcf</code></a>\nfeat: Support us mREP endpoint for Batch Prediction, Training, and\nOnline Pre...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/243ca19c2b71c2fe1be727cba878ae7e6703eae3\"><code>243ca19</code></a>\nfix: Send display_name when creating a sandbox environment\ntemplate.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/475024cdb47856cf97e1fab21e761062f5abe4f7\"><code>475024c</code></a>\nchore: Remove sandbox tool declarations from SDK AgentConfig\ndisplay.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/dbcf815680812e1beee23e15c20f12a435ace47b\"><code>dbcf815</code></a>\nfix: Depend on the <code>autogen</code> distribution instead of\n<code>ag2</code> for the AG2 integr...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/f93c45555512a3f3f27441194cbc8383b36fc358\"><code>f93c455</code></a>\nfix: Merge sandbox-only turns in SDK-side interaction-to-AgentData\nconversion.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/e46d239d90a9526745c3bc6d7d6ad9f6a043d7ee\"><code>e46d239</code></a>\nchore: Auto-construct <code>inference_configs</code> for\n<code>create_evaluation_run</code> with `a...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/commit/a16fc0df5472fc0ca6f063bb0b3c4cdb2995c131\"><code>a16fc0d</code></a>\nfix: GenAI client - Resolve opentelemetry-resourcedetector-gcp\ndependency error</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-aiplatform/compare/v1.162.0...v1.163.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `google-genai` from 2.14.0 to 2.17.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/releases\">google-genai's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.17.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.16.0...v2.17.0\">2.17.0</a>\n(2026-08-06)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add the Gemini Robotics ER 2 Preview model (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/61d4645c6f7acab5fdc1dd6a4f6943fe8c937347\">61d4645</a>)</li>\n<li>Add TOO_MANY_TOOL_CALLS to FinishReason enum. (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/a8ec86eab28c2806205fc8ec746b492110113c44\">a8ec86e</a>)</li>\n<li>Add top-level errors array to Interaction resource (iAPI) (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c74505b03f53e5bf54b0aed5741267f00703d218\">c74505b</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add propertyOrdering auto-population for ResponseSchema and\nResponseJsonSchema for Dotnet SDK (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/3ec20812f4e6228bfa8dc766167ede2e1f925526\">3ec2081</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix interactions (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/80d80ffb98e95b0c62590e5593df47c74ee6e0b7\">80d80ff</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.16.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f03ecfd7734e08b60d7ea5f2123152ff1b6bdfbf\">f03ecfd</a>)</li>\n<li>Update GenerateVideos docstrings and samples (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/c41ba1163f4bc7cb90d913674d1ba481d18d1248\">c41ba11</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.16.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.15.0...v2.16.0\">2.16.0</a>\n(2026-07-29)</h2>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add environment resource (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/615b6c3795f3ac005a7ed9517ddc2c86b2b7a043\">615b6c3</a>)</li>\n<li>Support GoogleMaps Tool grounding_types places and routing (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/95a335d809d75b987303d5a52e533a938585b7b5\">95a335d</a>)</li>\n<li>Wire environment service into genai sdk (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/361292ea6b5bfab276cbd6d55e7969119f9821ee\">361292e</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Communicate on upcoming updates in the next major version (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/f63b366babf7e8549b15a7afa02c035ec78078a1\">f63b366</a>)</li>\n<li>Regenerate docs for 2.15.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/commit/7c0e1bb49a087ce1ac658ab494528379393b728a\">7c0e1bb</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>v2.15.0</h2>\n<h2><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/googleapis/python-genai/compare/v2.14.